  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Phone Never Leaves the Window",
    "overview": "Bergamota is a native macOS SwiftUI app whose look is the Bergamota identity carried from the phone's boot screens onto the Mac: a paper work area, ink type, and a lime rail with the identity's 14 pt halftone dots standing beside every section. The rail holds the phone's state in Archivo 900, what the app is doing, Newton in halftone rising from its foot, and an ink console panel with the next boots. The work area does the section's job on quiet paper panels.\n\nDensity is that of a working instrument watched for hours: mono values, hairline-ruled rows, few colours, each with a job (leaf = iOS up and primary action, amber = ABL fastboot and waiting, alert red = anything that writes the phone or fails, lime = the stage). In the dark appearance paper and ink swap; the lime stage and the ink console do not change. The system refuses a dashboard of cards where the phone's state is one card among many.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One lime state rail (inspector column, 290-420 pt, 330 ideal) beside every page; hidden, its state falls back to a pill in the sidebar foot.",
      "Paper/ink work area with flat hairline panels; no shadows anywhere.",
      "Archivo 900 at 112% width for state words, page titles and big numbers; JetBrains Mono for every value; SF Pro for labels and controls.",
      "Halftone as the only decoration: the lime dot ground and the ink dissolve.",
      "Colour carries meaning (state, danger), never ornament.",
      "Native chrome stays native (sidebar List, toolbar, confirmation dialogs, .borderedProminent)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Colour-Is-State Rule",
        "body": "A colour on screen names a phone state or a consequence. Decorative use of leaf, amber, alert or lime is a defect.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red-Writes Rule",
        "body": "Alert red marks exactly what writes the phone (flash userdata, boot, logo) and failures; it also always asks first (typed or dialog confirmation).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink-Under-Lime Rule",
        "body": "On the lime stage every mark (type, rules, underline, progress) is ink; lime on lime vanishes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three Voices Rule",
        "body": "Archivo says what state; mono says what value; SF Pro says what to do. Never set a value in SF Pro or a label in Archivo.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Monospaced Digits Rule",
        "body": "Live numbers use .monospacedDigit() so they do not shimmer while metrics refresh.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-Hairline Rule",
        "body": "Separation comes from fill and a 1 pt rule stroke, never a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the State Rail visible beside every page; when hidden, show the state pill in the sidebar foot.",
      "Do set page titles, state words and big numbers in Archivo 900 at 112% width through BFont.display; values, paths, logs and commands in BFont.mono.",
